🚀 Day 15 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 15 – 3Sum.

This problem strengthened my understanding of the Sorting + Two Pointers technique and showed me how to efficiently solve triplet-based problems while avoiding duplicate answers.

💡 Approach: Sorting + Two Pointers

I first sorted the array, which allowed me to use the Two Pointers approach efficiently.

For each element:

I fixed one element as the first number of the triplet.
Then I placed two pointers (left and right) on the remaining part of the array.
Depending on the current sum:
If the sum was less than 0, I moved the left pointer forward.
If the sum was greater than 0, I moved the right pointer backward.
If the sum was 0, I stored the triplet and skipped duplicate elements to ensure unique answers.

This reduced the brute-force O(n³) solution to an optimized O(n²) approach.

📚 What I Learned:
✅ Applying Sorting + Two Pointers together
✅ Reducing time complexity from O(n³) to O(n²)
✅ Handling duplicate elements to avoid repeated triplets
✅ Using pointer movement based on the current sum
✅ Strengthening problem-solving skills for array-based interview questions

